\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The moving throat at $t=0$ is the Lorentz-contracted drainhole. (a)~The $\chi $ contour just inside the throat, at rest and at $p=0.45$, the latter on its analytic ellipse; the fainter ellipses continue the law to $v=0.7$ and $0.95$. (b)~Axis ratio (along/across the motion) against the boost speed $v=p/\sqrt  {m^2+p^2}$, on $1/\gamma =\sqrt  {1-v^2}$ drawn to the disc limit $v=1$. (c)~The residual: below $6\times 10^{-5}$ at every $v$ and at three contour levels. The outcome: the boosted data carry exactly the special-relativistic shape, with the scalar in motion, and both constraints hold at the exact solution's discretisation floor.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:boost_contraction}{{2}{5}{The moving throat at $t=0$ is the Lorentz-contracted drainhole. (a)~The $\chi $ contour just inside the throat, at rest and at $p=\clmSpiralMomentumFlyby $, the latter on its analytic ellipse; the fainter ellipses continue the law to $v=0.7$ and $0.95$. (b)~Axis ratio (along/across the motion) against the boost speed $v=p/\sqrt {m^2+p^2}$, on $1/\gamma =\sqrt {1-v^2}$ drawn to the disc limit $v=1$. (c)~The residual: below $\clmBoostAxisResidual $ at every $v$ and at three contour levels. The outcome: the boosted data carry exactly the special-relativistic shape, with the scalar in motion, and both constraints hold at the exact solution's discretisation floor}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces The run matrix: $103$ of the packed evolutions---the wormhole pairs on constraint-solved data, momentum carried by the exact Lorentz boost (Sec.~\ref {sec:model:boost})---in groups, each varying one knob against a named reference or repeating one; per-run lines are in the shipped registry. Left: the single throat and the initial-data machinery. Right: the binaries and their controls. Unless stated, $a=2$, $m=1$ ($R_{\min }=3.89$), $\sigma =-1$, $d=12$ and $L=64$ ($128$ for binaries deeper than level 3).}}{5}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:matrix}{{III}{5}{The run matrix: $\clmDetRunsTotal $ of the packed evolutions---the wormhole pairs on constraint-solved data, momentum carried by the exact Lorentz boost (Sec.~\ref {sec:model:boost})---in groups, each varying one knob against a named reference or repeating one; per-run lines are in the shipped registry. Left: the single throat and the initial-data machinery. Right: the binaries and their controls. Unless stated, $a=\clmThroatA $, $m=\clmThroatM $ ($R_{\min }=\clmRstarShort $), $\sigma =\clmMergerSign $, $d=\clmPairSeparation $ and $L=\clmBoxL $ ($\clmBigBoxL $ for binaries deeper than level 3)}{table.3}{}}
