\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The waveform gallery: one row per scenario on one retarded clock. Left: $r\,\mathrm  {Re}\,\Psi _4$ of the dominant mode at the innermost sphere, each row on its own scale; row (a) is the $\varepsilon _2=0.05$ arm, with the ringdown fit of Sec.~\ref {sec:single:gw} dashed (period $20.6\,M$). Caps mark where the drawn record ends: the collapsing throat before its numerical floor exceeds $14\%$ of the burst peak; the fly-by at its trust window ($t-R=67.6$), the plunge at its own. Row (b) is the same head-on rerun in an $L=512$ box with spheres to $R=150$, clean to the clock's edge. The merger runs through remnant ringdown, with one linear bridge across a leg seam. Grey under (b)--(d): the vacuum controls, black holes at the same $d$ and $p$ on bare punctures, on the same scale: the vacuum head-on rings $5.4\times $ lower and crests later (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:wave}); the vacuum merger peaks at the drainhole merger's retarded time, $3.0\times $ lower; the vacuum fly-by radiates one cycle as the holes swing away from periapsis, $6.7\times $ below the fly-by's arch. Right: the amplitude envelope at every sphere on its own retarded time (ink to faint, inner to outer)---the upper envelope of $|r\Psi _4|$ for the complex $(2,2)$ modes, the analytic-signal envelope for the real $(2,0)$ modes---which folds onto one curve for a signal moving at $c$ and falling as $1/r$. Gold dots: the correlated wavefront. The quoted $v/c$ is the whole-waveform lag between neighbouring spheres (Sec.~\ref {sec:controls:bbh}), the plunge's the burst-peak lag: throat $0.94/0.97/0.95$, head-on $0.89/0.94/0.96$, merger $0.86/0.88/0.94$, fly-by $0.91/1.00/1.00$, plunge $0.83$. Movies of the far-zone head-on, whose remnant spreads with the coordinates while its area holds, and of the vacuum head-on and fly-by: Videos~11 \href  {https://youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}}, 8 \href  {https://youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}} and~9 \href  {https://youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}}.}}{15}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_gallery}{{8}{15}{The waveform gallery: one row per scenario on one retarded clock. Left: $r\,\mathrm {Re}\,\Psi _4$ of the dominant mode at the innermost sphere, each row on its own scale; row (a) is the $\varepsilon _2=\clmGwSeedStrong $ arm, with the ringdown fit of Sec.~\ref {sec:single:gw} dashed (period $\clmGwThroatPeriod \,M$). Caps mark where the drawn record ends: the collapsing throat before its numerical floor exceeds $\clmGwDrawFloorFrac \%$ of the burst peak; the fly-by at its trust window ($t-R=\clmGwDrawFlybyRetarded $), the plunge at its own. Row (b) is the same head-on rerun in an $L=\clmFarzoneBoxL $ box with spheres to $R=\clmFarzoneOuterR $, clean to the clock's edge. The merger runs through remnant ringdown, with one linear bridge across a leg seam. Grey under (b)--(d): the vacuum controls, black holes at the same $d$ and $p$ on bare punctures, on the same scale: the vacuum head-on rings $\clmBbhHeadonAmpRatio \times $ lower and crests later (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:wave}); the vacuum merger peaks at the drainhole merger's retarded time, $\clmGwVacMergerPeakRatio \times $ lower; the vacuum fly-by radiates one cycle as the holes swing away from periapsis, $\clmGwVacPassPeakRatio \times $ below the fly-by's arch. Right: the amplitude envelope at every sphere on its own retarded time (ink to faint, inner to outer)---the upper envelope of $|r\Psi _4|$ for the complex $(2,2)$ modes, the analytic-signal envelope for the real $(2,0)$ modes---which folds onto one curve for a signal moving at $c$ and falling as $1/r$. Gold dots: the correlated wavefront. The quoted $v/c$ is the whole-waveform lag between neighbouring spheres (Sec.~\ref {sec:controls:bbh}), the plunge's the burst-peak lag: throat $\clmGwSpeedThroatA /\clmGwSpeedThroatB /\clmGwSpeedThroatC $, head-on $\clmGwSpeedHeadonA /\clmGwSpeedHeadonB /\clmGwSpeedHeadonC $, merger $\clmGwSpeedSpiralA /\clmGwSpeedSpiralB /\clmGwSpeedSpiralC $, fly-by $\clmGwSpeedFlybyA /\clmGwSpeedFlybyB /\clmGwSpeedFlybyC $, plunge $\clmGwSpeedPlunge $. Movies of the far-zone head-on, whose remnant spreads with the coordinates while its area holds, and of the vacuum head-on and fly-by: Videos~11 \href {https://youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}}, 8 \href {https://youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}} and~9 \href {https://youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}}}{figure.8}{}}
