\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Convergence. (a)~The static throat from exact data at levels 2--4: the three-level factor $Q=(R_2-R_3)/(R_3-R_4)$ of its minimal areal radius against the orders $n=2$, 3, 4 (rules); the dip at $t=16$ is one level-2 dump. (b)~$|r\Psi _4^{22}|$ at $R=20$ of the $d=12$, $p=0.12$ pair with Bowen--York momentum (otherwise our data) at throat level 5, its difference from level 4, and the difference made by refining the wave zone to half the base cell. (c)~Radiated energy on each sphere over the outermost sphere's, against $R/M$: the head-on, the $d=6$ merger and the fly-by (ink) and two vacuum controls (grey). (d)~The far-zone head-on of Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}(b) at finest $\Delta x=1/16$ and $1/32$: $|r\Psi _4^{20}|$ at $R=10$ and the two levels' difference, at most $0.5\%$ of its peak. Both form the common MOTS at $t=18$, its $R$ and $M_{\rm  MS}$ equal to $0.08\%$, and their energies at $R=10$ differ by $0.3\%$; a third level, $\Delta x=1/64$, so far run to $t=67$, shrinks that difference at order $1.7$. The outcome: the scheme converges at order $3.0$--$3.3$, a binary's waveform is resolved to $0.4\%$ of its peak, and the energy converges in extraction radius and in resolution.}}{21}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convergence}{{11}{21}{Convergence. (a)~The static throat from exact data at levels 2--4: the three-level factor $Q=(R_2-R_3)/(R_3-R_4)$ of its minimal areal radius against the orders $n=2$, 3, 4 (rules); the dip at $t=16$ is one level-2 dump. (b)~$|r\Psi _4^{22}|$ at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTwenty $ of the $d=12$, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumProd $ pair with Bowen--York momentum (otherwise our data) at throat level 5, its difference from level 4, and the difference made by refining the wave zone to half the base cell. (c)~Radiated energy on each sphere over the outermost sphere's, against $R/M$: the head-on, the $d=6$ merger and the fly-by (ink) and two vacuum controls (grey). (d)~The far-zone head-on of Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}(b) at finest $\Delta x=1/\clmConvFzDxLo $ and $1/\clmConvFzDxMid $: $|r\Psi _4^{20}|$ at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTen $ and the two levels' difference, at most $\clmConvFzPsiDiff \%$ of its peak. Both form the common MOTS at $t=\clmConvFzMotsTime $, its $R$ and $M_{\rm MS}$ equal to $\clmConvFzMotsDiff \%$, and their energies at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTen $ differ by $\clmConvFzEnergyDiff \%$; a third level, $\Delta x=1/\clmConvFzDxHi $, so far run to $t=\clmConvFzFineTime $, shrinks that difference at order $\clmConvFzOrder $. The outcome: the scheme converges at order $\clmConvOrderEvolLo $--$\clmConvOrderEvolHi $, a binary's waveform is resolved to $\clmConvPsiLevelDiff \%$ of its peak, and the energy converges in extraction radius and in resolution}{figure.11}{}}
