\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Constraint evolution of every run the main-text figures draw, each at the highest refinement level it was run at (named in each panel's key): $L^2$ norms of the Hamiltonian ($\mathcal  {H}$, ink) and momentum ($\mathcal  {M}$, grey dashed) constraints, box averages on the base grid ($\Delta x=0.5$; $2$ on the octant of (d)) that compare only within one box (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:diagnostics}). (a),(b)~The lone throat of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_throat}: level 4 for the unkicked throat and $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ ($+10^{-2}$ stopped by hand, dot), level 3 for $\pm 10^{-3}$ and $\pm 0.1$ (dash = sign, weight = amplitude, grey = no kick, crosses = deaths). At $t=0$ the norms carry the exact data's discretisation floor plus the kick's own defect, $0.090\,|\varepsilon |$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:model:seeds}), which feeds $\mathcal  {M}$ within the first steps; the $|\varepsilon |\le 10^{-2}$ arms then follow the unkicked norms to $5.4\%$ until the fates part, while $\varepsilon =\pm 0.1$ starts $3$--$6\times $ high and dies in a one-step overflow at the compactified origin. (c)~The pure-quadrupole collapse of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_collapse} (gold, its MOTS from $t=33$; dotted, its trust window, $t=60$): the late rise comes after it. (d)~The inflating throat of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_inflation} to $t=218$. (e)~The head-on chain of Fig.~\ref {fig:headon_collapse} with its ladder (era rules at the restarts, levels per era): the level-5 leg's overrun dies of the censored interior NaN at $t=38.845$ (cross) with its norm below its value at formation (gold rule, $t=18$). (f)~The $d=6$ merger chain of Fig.~\ref {fig:spiral_collapse}: the used legs in ink, every failed arm in grey to its death cross (the level-6 and level-7 restarts dashed; times in Fig.~\ref {fig:spiral_collapse}(d)). At every end, hand stop and death alike, the Hamiltonian norm sits at or below its start: each failure is the interior NaN of Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:wall}, not a constraint blow-up. (g)~The $p=0.60$ plunge, level 4 throughout: the floor-free extension (grey) dies of the merged core's cell NaN at $t=55.5$ with its norm at its floor, the $\chi $-floor leg carries the record to $t=100$, and a level-5 restart (grey dashed) crosses the merger with clean norms; dotted, the trust window ($t=80$). (h)~The $p=0.45$ scatterer: the norms sit on their floor through the pass and grow as the mouths inflate; rules, the trust window ($t=67.6$) and the wave gate ($t=87.6$). The needles on (g), (h) and the $p=0.25$ arm, never on the head-on or $d=6$ chains, are the base-grid norm reading the moving throats' $\chi $ pits: on the $p=0.25$ verification pair four cells next to the pits carry $99.99\%$ of a needle while the level-3 solution is clean, and neither $\max |K|$ nor the waves carry a counterpart.}}{22}{figure.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:constraints}{{12}{22}{Constraint evolution of every run the main-text figures draw, each at the highest refinement level it was run at (named in each panel's key): $L^2$ norms of the Hamiltonian ($\mathcal {H}$, ink) and momentum ($\mathcal {M}$, grey dashed) constraints, box averages on the base grid ($\Delta x=\clmDxBase $; $\clmFourDxBase $ on the octant of (d)) that compare only within one box (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:diagnostics}). (a),(b)~The lone throat of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_throat}: level 4 for the unkicked throat and $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ ($+10^{-2}$ stopped by hand, dot), level 3 for $\pm 10^{-3}$ and $\pm 0.1$ (dash = sign, weight = amplitude, grey = no kick, crosses = deaths). At $t=0$ the norms carry the exact data's discretisation floor plus the kick's own defect, $\clmSeedDefectBox \,|\varepsilon |$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:model:seeds}), which feeds $\mathcal {M}$ within the first steps; the $|\varepsilon |\le 10^{-2}$ arms then follow the unkicked norms to $\clmKickNormSpread \%$ until the fates part, while $\varepsilon =\pm 0.1$ starts $\clmCeilingHamLo $--$\clmCeilingHamHi \times $ high and dies in a one-step overflow at the compactified origin. (c)~The pure-quadrupole collapse of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_collapse} (gold, its MOTS from $t=\clmPureQuadMotsTime $; dotted, its trust window, $t=\clmPureQuadTrust $): the late rise comes after it. (d)~The inflating throat of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_inflation} to $t=\clmFourWall $. (e)~The head-on chain of Fig.~\ref {fig:headon_collapse} with its ladder (era rules at the restarts, levels per era): the level-5 leg's overrun dies of the censored interior NaN at $t=\clmHeadonCsmNanTime $ (cross) with its norm below its value at formation (gold rule, $t=\clmHeadonCsmMotsTime $). (f)~The $d=6$ merger chain of Fig.~\ref {fig:spiral_collapse}: the used legs in ink, every failed arm in grey to its death cross (the level-6 and level-7 restarts dashed; times in Fig.~\ref {fig:spiral_collapse}(d)). At every end, hand stop and death alike, the Hamiltonian norm sits at or below its start: each failure is the interior NaN of Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:wall}, not a constraint blow-up. (g)~The $p=\clmEgwPSixty $ plunge, level 4 throughout: the floor-free extension (grey) dies of the merged core's cell NaN at $t=\clmPSixtyExtDeath $ with its norm at its floor, the $\chi $-floor leg carries the record to $t=100$, and a level-5 restart (grey dashed) crosses the merger with clean norms; dotted, the trust window ($t=\clmPSixtyTrust $). (h)~The $p=\clmSpiralMomentumFlyby $ scatterer: the norms sit on their floor through the pass and grow as the mouths inflate; rules, the trust window ($t=\clmPFortyFiveTrust $) and the wave gate ($t=\clmEgwGateFortyFive $). The needles on (g), (h) and the $p=\clmSpiralMomentumTwentyFive $ arm, never on the head-on or $d=6$ chains, are the base-grid norm reading the moving throats' $\chi $ pits: on the $p=\clmSpiralMomentumTwentyFive $ verification pair four cells next to the pits carry $\clmNormPitShare \%$ of a needle while the level-3 solution is clean, and neither $\max |K|$ nor the waves carry a counterpart}{figure.12}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Top (channel):} The scalar channel on the $\Psi _4$ spheres. (a)~Fly-by energy through $R=30$ in units of the gravitational energy crossed by the end of the sphere's trusted record ($t=97.6$, $t-R=67.6$): gravitational (ink) and scalar with its physical sign (gold, Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}). The ratio $|E_\phi |/E_{\rm  GW}$ printed at each cut falls from $2.4$ at $t=60$ to $0.56$ over the whole record, as the gravitational burst arrives after the scalar one (Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}). (b)~Multipole content, fly-by: $\ell =1$ exceeds $\ell =0$ and $\ell =2$ by $10^{6.4}$. (c)~Validity window: $|F_\phi |$ at both spheres, each drawn to its retarded gate $t-R=67.6$. Past the blue rule ($t=60$) the inner sphere reads the inflating mouths' near field---its climb there has no counterpart at $R=30$ one light-crossing later---so that stretch is dashed and carries no claim; the $t=60$ window at $R=14$ gives $0.6$ in place of $2.4$. \emph  {Bottom (censorship):} Envelope of the scalar flux $|F_\phi |$, horizoned against horizonless arms: a running maximum over $25$ units, smoothed in log amplitude, since the raw flux changes sign every ${\sim }13$ units. (a)~The head-on chain's glued record at $R=10/14/18$. The common MOTS closes at $t=18$ (dotted); the remaining hair leaves as one $\ell =1$ pulse, cresting later at each sphere, then decays (dashed: fits over $t=30$--$80$, $\tau =22/38/73$). The rise before the rule is the open mouths' static hair, canonically ingoing; only the outgoing window is integrated. (b)~One sphere per fate (head-on and lone throat $R=18$, merger $R=20$, fly-by $R=30$): the merger, behind its horizon from $t=13$, decays like the head-on ($\tau =22$, dotted fit); the fly-by, horizonless, shows its burst's complete arch, drawn to $t-R=67.6$ (its trust window). Mid-grey: the lone throat twice---the $\varepsilon =+10^{-2}$ level-4{} collapse (solid), behind a MOTS from $t=11$, and the unkicked level-4{} throat (dotted), which inflates, horizonless, and grows in the monopole (counted to $t\approx 80$).}}{23}{figure.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scalar_channel}{{13}{23}{\emph {Top (channel):} The scalar channel on the $\Psi _4$ spheres. (a)~Fly-by energy through $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusOuter $ in units of the gravitational energy crossed by the end of the sphere's trusted record ($t=\clmGwScalarGateOuter $, $t-R=\clmFlybyTrustRetarded $): gravitational (ink) and scalar with its physical sign (gold, Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}). The ratio $|E_\phi |/E_{\rm GW}$ printed at each cut falls from $\clmGwScalarRatioSixty $ at $t=\clmGwScalarCut $ to $\clmGwScalarRatioFull $ over the whole record, as the gravitational burst arrives after the scalar one (Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}). (b)~Multipole content, fly-by: $\ell =1$ exceeds $\ell =0$ and $\ell =2$ by $10^{\clmGwScalarDipoleGap }$. (c)~Validity window: $|F_\phi |$ at both spheres, each drawn to its retarded gate $t-R=\clmFlybyTrustRetarded $. Past the blue rule ($t=\clmGwScalarCut $) the inner sphere reads the inflating mouths' near field---its climb there has no counterpart at $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusOuter $ one light-crossing later---so that stretch is dashed and carries no claim; the $t=\clmGwScalarCut $ window at $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusInner $ gives $\clmGwScalarRatioInner $ in place of $\clmGwScalarRatioSixty $. \emph {Bottom (censorship):} Envelope of the scalar flux $|F_\phi |$, horizoned against horizonless arms: a running maximum over $\clmGwEnvWindow $ units, smoothed in log amplitude, since the raw flux changes sign every ${\sim }\clmGwFluxSignStretch $ units. (a)~The head-on chain's glued record at $R=\clmGwHeadonRadiusA /\clmGwHeadonRadiusB /\clmGwHeadonRadiusC $. The common MOTS closes at $t=\clmHeadonCsmMotsTime $ (dotted); the remaining hair leaves as one $\ell =1$ pulse, cresting later at each sphere, then decays (dashed: fits over $t=\clmGwCensFitLo $--$\clmGwCensFitHi $, $\tau =\clmGwCensTauInner /\clmGwCensTauMid /\clmGwCensTauOuter $). The rise before the rule is the open mouths' static hair, canonically ingoing; only the outgoing window is integrated. (b)~One sphere per fate (head-on and lone throat $R=\clmGwHeadonRadiusC $, merger $R=\clmGwCensMergerRadius $, fly-by $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusOuter $): the merger, behind its horizon from $t=\clmMergerMotsTime $, decays like the head-on ($\tau =\clmGwCensMergerTau $, dotted fit); the fly-by, horizonless, shows its burst's complete arch, drawn to $t-R=\clmFlybyTrustRetarded $ (its trust window). Mid-grey: the lone throat twice---the $\varepsilon =\clmGwKickedEps $ level-\clmGwKickedLevel {} collapse (solid), behind a MOTS from $t=\clmGwKickedMotsTime $, and the unkicked level-\clmGwSingleLevel {} throat (dotted), which inflates, horizonless, and grows in the monopole (counted to $t\approx \clmGwSingleCountTime $)}{figure.13}{}}
\newlabel{fig:scalar_censorship}{{13}{23}{\emph {Top (channel):} The scalar channel on the $\Psi _4$ spheres. (a)~Fly-by energy through $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusOuter $ in units of the gravitational energy crossed by the end of the sphere's trusted record ($t=\clmGwScalarGateOuter $, $t-R=\clmFlybyTrustRetarded $): gravitational (ink) and scalar with its physical sign (gold, Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}). The ratio $|E_\phi |/E_{\rm GW}$ printed at each cut falls from $\clmGwScalarRatioSixty $ at $t=\clmGwScalarCut $ to $\clmGwScalarRatioFull $ over the whole record, as the gravitational burst arrives after the scalar one (Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}). (b)~Multipole content, fly-by: $\ell =1$ exceeds $\ell =0$ and $\ell =2$ by $10^{\clmGwScalarDipoleGap }$. (c)~Validity window: $|F_\phi |$ at both spheres, each drawn to its retarded gate $t-R=\clmFlybyTrustRetarded $. Past the blue rule ($t=\clmGwScalarCut $) the inner sphere reads the inflating mouths' near field---its climb there has no counterpart at $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusOuter $ one light-crossing later---so that stretch is dashed and carries no claim; the $t=\clmGwScalarCut $ window at $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusInner $ gives $\clmGwScalarRatioInner $ in place of $\clmGwScalarRatioSixty $. \emph {Bottom (censorship):} Envelope of the scalar flux $|F_\phi |$, horizoned against horizonless arms: a running maximum over $\clmGwEnvWindow $ units, smoothed in log amplitude, since the raw flux changes sign every ${\sim }\clmGwFluxSignStretch $ units. (a)~The head-on chain's glued record at $R=\clmGwHeadonRadiusA /\clmGwHeadonRadiusB /\clmGwHeadonRadiusC $. The common MOTS closes at $t=\clmHeadonCsmMotsTime $ (dotted); the remaining hair leaves as one $\ell =1$ pulse, cresting later at each sphere, then decays (dashed: fits over $t=\clmGwCensFitLo $--$\clmGwCensFitHi $, $\tau =\clmGwCensTauInner /\clmGwCensTauMid /\clmGwCensTauOuter $). The rise before the rule is the open mouths' static hair, canonically ingoing; only the outgoing window is integrated. (b)~One sphere per fate (head-on and lone throat $R=\clmGwHeadonRadiusC $, merger $R=\clmGwCensMergerRadius $, fly-by $R=\clmGwScalarRadiusOuter $): the merger, behind its horizon from $t=\clmMergerMotsTime $, decays like the head-on ($\tau =\clmGwCensMergerTau $, dotted fit); the fly-by, horizonless, shows its burst's complete arch, drawn to $t-R=\clmFlybyTrustRetarded $ (its trust window). Mid-grey: the lone throat twice---the $\varepsilon =\clmGwKickedEps $ level-\clmGwKickedLevel {} collapse (solid), behind a MOTS from $t=\clmGwKickedMotsTime $, and the unkicked level-\clmGwSingleLevel {} throat (dotted), which inflates, horizonless, and grows in the monopole (counted to $t\approx \clmGwSingleCountTime $)}{figure.13}{}}
